- CWE-184: Incomplete List of Disallowed Input
WHAT: Relying on a deny list of disallowed tags/characters (e.g., blocking specific `<script>` patterns) allows attackers to bypass filters using alternate encodings or characters, leading to unfiltered dangerous input.
WHY: Incomplete deny lists can miss malicious variants (e.g., mixed-language or Unicode code points), enabling XSS or other injection attacks despite apparent filtering.
HOW: Canonicalize (normalize) untrusted input first, then validate it using a strict allow list of known-safe tags/characters/patterns; reject anything not explicitly allowed and handle validation failures safely.
EXAMPLE (Python): Before: `if tag in ["<script>", "<img", "<a href"]:` (deny list). After: `if tag not in ["<b>", "<p>", "</p>"]:` then `raise ValueError("Invalid input tag")` for all other tags, after prior normalization.



